    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0545" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Defense Files: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of War</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >McCloy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of War</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stimson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-27">27 November 1943.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10065 (To Stimson from McCloy)</p>
                <p>Have had talks with Joint Chiefs and British on civil affairs matters and
                    discussions with others including President, Winant and Eden.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d336-f1"/> Feel that if British confirm agreement outlined in
                    my 10064 we have accomplished all that we have set out to do on civil affairs
                    matter. <pb facs="0546" n="444" xml:id="pg444"/> Though I have only been on
                    fringe of strategical discussions, it is clear that all decisions of important
                    matters are held up pending results Eastern conference<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d336-f2"/> to which I did not go though I was requested to stay on
                    here pending their return.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d336-f1" n="1" xml:id="d336-f1-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg351">pp. 351</ref>, <ref
                        target="#pg415">415</ref>, and telegram printed <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d336-f2" n="2" xml:id="d336-f2-content">
                <p>Conference at Tehran.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
